## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with SwiftUI basics, timer handling, accessibility, and simple persistence in a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- SwiftUI TimerPublisher and state management
- MVVM pattern with @ObservableObject and @Published
- UserDefaults for minimal persistence
- Accessibility: VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, color contrast
- Debouncing user input to prevent thrashing

## Code Example
```swift
class FocusTimerViewModel: ObservableObject {
  @Published var remaining: Int = 0
  @Published var isRunning: Bool = false
  private var cancellable: AnyCancellable?
  func start(duration: Int) {
    remaining = duration * 60
    isRunning = true
    cancellable = Timer.publish(every: 1, on: .main, in: .common)
      .autoconnect()
      .sink { [weak self] _ in
        guard let self = self else { return }
        if self.remaining > 0 { self.remaining -= 1 } else { self.isRunning = false }
      }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle timer accuracy when the app is backgrounded?
- How would you scale to more than 3 presets and persist per-preset state?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses offline-first design, delta-based syncing, and conflict handling under intermittent connectivity, which are critical in collaboration apps used by teams.

## Key Concepts

- Core Data data model for Comment and Patch objects
- Delta/patch format including baseVersion, changes, and timestamps
- Reconciliation strategy (latest-writer-wins or server-validated merges)
- Robust test plan for offline edits, re-connect, and concurrency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Swift-like pseudocode: apply a patch to a Comment
func apply(patch: Patch, to comment: inout Comment) {
    // Validate base version matches current state
    guard patch.baseVersion == comment.version else {
        // Handle conflict resolution
        resolveConflict(patch: patch, comment: &comment)
        return
    }

    // Apply delta changes
    for change in patch.changes {
        switch change.type {
        case .insert:
            comment.text.insert(change.text, at: change.position)
        case .delete:
            comment.text.removeSubrange(change.range)
        case .replace:
            comment.text.replaceSubrange(change.range, with: change.text)
        }
    }

    // Update version and timestamps
    comment.version += 1
    comment.updatedAt = Date()
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
